A first structural fact is now clear: each graph band already carries an exact constant-rank staged elimination (`rank_C`), so a localized certificate can be built from bandwise row operations if the remaining compatibility equations reduce through earlier stages. I’m checking that route next and, in parallel within the same engine, testing whether the recovered pickles actually contain source-to-NF traces (the producing script normally discarded them). This determines whether Step 1 can be promoted honestly or must remain a precise blocker.
